{"id":"e6df3beb84e45a4e","group":"58","path":"58/batch01/58-df-baker.md","title":"Baker Linear Form","display":"df-baker — Baker Linear Form","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-baker","aliases":["58-df-baker","Baker Linear Form"],"display":"df-baker — Baker Linear Form","depends_on":[]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-baker"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-baker</span><span>Baker Linear Form</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-baker — Baker Linear Form"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<span class=\"property-null\">无</span>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\mathbb N\">\\(n\\in\\mathbb N\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Lambda\\in\\mathbb C\">\\(\\Lambda\\in\\mathbb C\\)</span>。</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\vec\\alpha\\in(\\overline{\\mathbb Q}^{\\times})^n\">\\(\\vec\\alpha\\in(\\overline{\\mathbb Q}^{\\times})^n\\)</span>、<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\vec\\beta\\in\\overline{\\mathbb Q}^{\\,n+1}\">\\(\\vec\\beta\\in\\overline{\\mathbb Q}^{\\,n+1}\\)</span>、<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\vec\\ell\\in\\mathbb C^n\">\\(\\vec\\ell\\in\\mathbb C^n\\)</span>；有限序数 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n=\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}\">\\(n=\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}\\)</span> 是前后两个长度为 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\">\\(n\\)</span> 的元组的共同定义域。</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\forall i\\in n\\;(\\exp(\\vec\\ell(i))=\\vec\\alpha(i))\">\\(\\forall i\\in n\\;(\\exp(\\vec\\ell(i))=\\vec\\alpha(i))\\)</span>。</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{BakerLinearForm}_S\\subseteq V^5\">\\(\\mathrm{BakerLinearForm}_S\\subseteq V^5\\)</span> 是下述定义的谓词。</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}baker}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{BakerLinearForm}_S(\\Lambda,n,\\vec\\alpha,\\vec\\beta,\\vec\\ell)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\leftrightarrow\nn\\in\\mathbb N\n\\land\\vec\\alpha\\in(\\overline{\\mathbb Q}^{\\times})^n\n\\land\\vec\\beta\\in\\overline{\\mathbb Q}^{\\,n+1}\n\\land\\vec\\ell\\in\\mathbb C^n\n\\land\\forall i\\in n\\;(e^{\\vec\\ell(i)}=\\vec\\alpha(i))\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{23mm}{}\\land\n\\Lambda=\\vec\\beta(0)+\\sum_{i\\in n}\\vec\\beta(i+1)\\vec\\ell(i).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}baker}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{BakerLinearForm}_S(\\Lambda,n,\\vec\\alpha,\\vec\\beta,\\vec\\ell)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\leftrightarrow\nn\\in\\mathbb N\n\\land\\vec\\alpha\\in(\\overline{\\mathbb Q}^{\\times})^n\n\\land\\vec\\beta\\in\\overline{\\mathbb Q}^{\\,n+1}\n\\land\\vec\\ell\\in\\mathbb C^n\n\\land\\forall i\\in n\\;(e^{\\vec\\ell(i)}=\\vec\\alpha(i))\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{23mm}{}\\land\n\\Lambda=\\vec\\beta(0)+\\sum_{i\\in n}\\vec\\beta(i+1)\\vec\\ell(i).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Baker's theorem: linear forms in logarithms are either zero or have absolute lower bound</li>\n<li>The three coefficient/logarithm tuples are now typed inside the defining equivalence; the earlier indexed typography left them unconstrained object terms.</li>\n<li>Effective lower bounds for linear combinations of logarithms of algebraic numbers</li>\n<li>Applications: exponential Diophantine equations, Mordell conjecture, class number problem</li>\n<li>Baker's method: reducing bounds via Siegel's lemma and lattice reduction</li>\n<li>Modern form: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"|(m+1)\\log 2 + n\\log 3| &gt; c \\cdot 2^{-10^6}\">\\(|(m+1)\\log 2 + n\\log 3| &gt; c \\cdot 2^{-10^6}\\)</span> for non-trivial <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"m, n\">\\(m, n\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Baker, Transcendental Number Theory</li>\n<li>Waldschmidt, Diophantine Approximation on Linear Algebraic Groups</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[],"math":[{"tex":"n\\in\\mathbb N","display":false},{"tex":"\\Lambda\\in\\mathbb C","display":false},{"tex":"\\vec\\alpha\\in(\\overline{\\mathbb Q}^{\\times})^n","display":false},{"tex":"\\vec\\beta\\in\\overline{\\mathbb Q}^{\\,n+1}","display":false},{"tex":"\\vec\\ell\\in\\mathbb C^n","display":false},{"tex":"n=\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}","display":false},{"tex":"n","display":false},{"tex":"\\forall i\\in n\\;(\\exp(\\vec\\ell(i))=\\vec\\alpha(i))","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{BakerLinearForm}_S\\subseteq V^5","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathrm{df\\text{-}baker}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{BakerLinearForm}_S(\\Lambda,n,\\vec\\alpha,\\vec\\beta,\\vec\\ell)\\\\\n&\\quad\\leftrightarrow\nn\\in\\mathbb N\n\\land\\vec\\alpha\\in(\\overline{\\mathbb Q}^{\\times})^n\n\\land\\vec\\beta\\in\\overline{\\mathbb Q}^{\\,n+1}\n\\land\\vec\\ell\\in\\mathbb C^n\n\\land\\forall i\\in n\\;(e^{\\vec\\ell(i)}=\\vec\\alpha(i))\\\\\n&\\hspace{23mm}{}\\land\n\\Lambda=\\vec\\beta(0)+\\sum_{i\\in n}\\vec\\beta(i+1)\\vec\\ell(i).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"|(m+1)\\log 2 + n\\log 3| > c \\cdot 2^{-10^6}","display":false},{"tex":"m, n","display":false}],"bytes":1805,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-165","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch01/58-df-baker.md|58-df-baker]]（batch01）"}],"outgoing":[]}